{"text": "OFFICE OF ADMINISTRATIVE HEARINGS - for the Employment Security Department\nDocket 04-2025-UI-118204     Claimant ID 7700418823     SSN xxx-xx-8373\nClaimant: TSEHAY WOLDEMICHAEL          Employer: QUAYSIDE VALET & PARKING, INC.\nTelephone hearing, November 6, 2025, 1:15 p.m. Recording begins.\n\nJUDGE FOSSE: This is Administrative Law Judge Bernadine Fosse. The issue is whether the claimant was discharged for misconduct under RCW 50.20.066. On the line I have the claimant, her representative from the Unemployment Law Clinic of Puget Sound, and for the employer, Mr. Lunsford. Ms. Woldemichael, I'm calling you at 206-555-0114, is that a good number if we're disconnected?\n\nCLAIMANT: Yes. That is my daughter's phone. Kalkidan. Mine is broken.\n\nJUDGE: And your mailing address is still 8815 Renton Avenue South, Apartment 204, Seattle, 98118?\n\nCLAIMANT: Yes. Rainier Beach.\n\nJUDGE: Mr. Lunsford, your full name and position.\n\nMR. LUNSFORD: Trevor Lunsford, regional operations manager, Quayside Valet. We let her go on September 12th for a third no-call, no-show. It's in Exhibit 3, the points sheet. She was at seven and a half points.\n\nJUDGE: Ms. Woldemichael, what was your job and rate of pay?\n\nCLAIMANT: Cashier at the garage on Pike Street, four years. $21.40 an hour.\n\nJUDGE: Tell me about September 11.\n\nCLAIMANT: That day is our New Year. Enkutatash. I am Ethiopian Orthodox. Every year I ask for this day and I get it. This year in August I asked the new supervisor and he said \"put it in the app.\" I put it in the app. I have the picture, it says \"pending.\" Nobody answered me.\n\nMR. LUNSFORD: Pending isn't approved, Your Honor. The handbook is clear.\n\nJUDGE: You'll have your turn. Go on, ma'am.\n\nCLAIMANT: The other two times, in July, I was at the hospital. I was pregnant and I lost the baby. I brought the paper from the doctor on July 22. He did not take the points away.\n\nJUDGE: Mr. Lunsford, did the employer receive medical documentation in July?\n\nMR. LUNSFORD: I'd have to check with HR. I will say, when she was hired her work permit was a temporary one, and there was a gap when it expired, so there's history of paperwork being late.\n\nCLAIMANT: I am an asylee. My card was renewed. USCIS was late, not me. I never worked one day without permission.\n\nJUDGE: That isn't the issue before me and I'm not going to consider it. Under WAC 192-150-205 the employer has the burden. Mr. Lunsford, does the company have anything in writing showing the September 11 request was denied before the shift?\n\nMR. LUNSFORD: Not in front of me.\n\nJUDGE: All right. I'll leave the record open until November 13 for the app screenshot and the July doctor's note. Send them to the fax on the notice. Ms. Woldemichael, your weekly benefit amount if you prevail is $612, going back to the week of 9/14/2025. A written order will be mailed. We're off the record at 1:52.", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "486 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["TSEHAY WOLDEMICHAEL", "Kalkidan", "Trevor Lunsford", "Bernadine Fosse", "MR. LUNSFORD", "JUDGE", "Ms. Woldemichael"], "companies": ["QUAYSIDE VALET & PARKING", "Unemployment Law Clinic of Puget Sound", "USCIS"]}, "topics": {"places": ["Seattle", "Renton", "Puget Sound", "Pike Street"], "health": ["pregnant", "lost the baby", "hospital", "doctor's note"], "sensitive": ["asylee", "WAC 192-150-205", "September 11"], "names": ["Tsehay", "Bernadine", "Kalkidan", "Trevor", "Lunsford", "Woldemichael"]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "topicErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.3999999985098839, "modelMs": 20935.29999999702, "topicMs": 26949.39999999851, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "card_partial", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "names", "sensitive_topics"], "detections": [{"start": 44, "end": 74, "